<title>USA: Court rules against EG&amp;G in patent suit.</title>
<headline>Court rules against EG&amp;G in patent suit.</headline>
<dateline>WELLESLEY, Mass. 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>EG&amp;G Inc said on Thursday a U.S. District Court ruled against it in a patent infringement suit raised by plaintiffs Lunar Corp and the University of Alabama's Birmingham Research Foundation.</p>
<p>The court awarded the plaintiffs $4.2 million and instituted an injunction against EG&amp;G's astrophysics division from manufacturing and selling an type of scanner used in security applications, the company said.</p>
<p>EG&amp;G said the injunction covered only scanners sold to non-government customers in the United States and would have limited impact on overal sales of EG&amp;G security systems.</p>
<p>The company also said it was reviewing the judgement and considering if an appeal was appropriate.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
